Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:59:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Eterna Forest's trees past its edge on the wider field
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The wider field sees about 12 tiles each side of the player, the DS's 8.
By the forest's east edge (its way out to Route 205) the view went past
the last of its maps, where there is no map, and showed black. With the
player in the half of a map by the matrix's left or right edge, the maps
of that column are drawn again past it, mirrored left to right about the
edge (their props too), so the trees by the edge go on past it. A
mirrored model's faces turn the other way, so its materials' culled side
is swapped while it's drawn. Only for the matrices listed (Eterna
Forest's): past a town's edge, mirrored houses would look wrong.
---
